<title>USA: Corning sells Franklin Health to management.</title>
<headline>Corning sells Franklin Health to management.</headline>
<dateline>UPPER SADDLE RIVER, N.J. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Managed care service provider Franklin Health announced Wednesday that its management purchased the company from Corning Inc in a management buy-back.</p>
<p>The new company, owned by management, outside directors and private equity fund Willis Stein &amp; Partners, will be called Franklin Health Inc. the company said.</p>
<p>Corning will not retain any ownership in the business, it added.</p>
